  "rationale": "THIS FILE IS A MEASUREMENT, NOT A BALANCE CLAIM. release-plan.md forbids a balance claim before 0.5.0 and none is made here: the numbers below say what this build does, not what it should do, and every constant behind them is still tuningStatus untuned. Re-recorded after the wiring campaign (PR #201, merged 574e4e65) gave every effect primitive a node-driven consumer, made magnitudes signed so a node can express a cost, and added a casting claimant. The academic rates -- research-rate, teach-rate, scribe-rate -- were previously consumed only from god blessing constants, so what a mage knew moved no rate; they are now fed from authored node effects. Every knowledge metric moved up, which is the expected direction. The exception points the other way and is the finding: referenceNodesGainedFinalQuarter fell 8.43 to 4.35, so the universe learns more overall and gains less late -- it front-loads and exhausts the reachable set sooner. The ceiling did not move, it is reached earlier. A re-seal was attempted first and refused, correctly, because these are behaviour moves and not provenance. Verified live by ablation rather than by the consumption check alone: amplifying each primitive's authored magnitudes x100 moves the run for all three academic rates, where it was byte-identical before the campaign. The pool remains partly degenerate -- several scripted strategies are still effect-degenerate on most god verbs, so a multi-strategy mean here is a summary over arms that do very different things, and POOL_BUILD_LIMITS still bounds what a pairwise matrix taken now would mean.",
